Threat Hunt — Suspicious Process Spawning (Living-off-the-Land)
Hypothesis
An attacker is attempting to execute a malicious payload by exploiting a "Living-off-the-Land" (LotL) technique
. The hypothesis is that a common office application (e.g., Word) has been weaponized to spawn a system shell or scripting interpreter to download further malware
.
Data Source
Sysmon: Event ID 1 (Process Creation) to identify parent-child relationships
.
Windows Security: Event ID 4688 (New process created) with command-line auditing enabled
.
KQL (Microsoft Sentinel/Defender)
// Hunting for Word/Excel spawning PowerShell or CMD
DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFileName in~ ("winword.exe", "excel.exe", "outlook.exe")
| where FileName in~ ("powershell.exe", "cmd.exe", "wscript.exe", "mshta.exe")
| project TimeGenerated, DeviceName, InitiatingProcessFileName, FileName, ProcessCommandLine
Logic: This query identifies high-fidelity indicators of an initial access or execution phase by looking for productivity apps launching system tools
.
SPL (Splunk)
index=windows_logs (EventCode=1 OR EventCode=4688) 
ParentImage="*winword.exe" (Image="*powershell.exe" OR Image="*cmd.exe")
| table _time, host, ParentImage, Image, CommandLine
Logic: Filters for instances where Microsoft Word is the direct parent of a command shell, which is a rare behavior in normal business operations
.
Findings
During the hunt, a workstation was flagged where winword.exe spawned powershell.exe with a -enc (encoded) command
. Forensic analysis revealed the user opened a phishing attachment, triggering the execution of a fileless payload in memory
.
False Positives
Administrative Macros: Legacy Excel documents used by finance departments that legitimately call system commands
.
Security Tooling: EDR or inventory agents that may occasionally trigger process events during updates
.
MITRE ATT&CK
Tactic: Execution (TA0002).
Technique: Command and Scripting Interpreter: PowerShell (T1059.001)
.
Detection Improvement
Sigma Rule: Implement a rule to alert on any office process spawning an interpreter
.
GPO Hardening: Disable macros for all users except those with a specific business requirement
.
